  "step_2": "The verbal report states: 'Die Risiko-Unterschiede wirken auf mich marginal. Jedoch will ich anmerken, dass ich bei Wahlmöglichkeit weder auf A noch auf B eingegangen wäre.' This translates to: 'The risk differences affect me marginally. However, I would like to note that I would not have chosen either A or B.' The individual acknowledges that risk differences are marginal, implying they did not consider the differences in outcomes or probabilities as significant. There is no mention of comparing maximum or minimum outcomes, nor any reference to preferring a lottery based on its favorable outcome. The individual does not describe any deliberation involving the outcomes of the lotteries, especially not the maximum or minimum values. The justification for the choice (or lack thereof) is absent — the individual simply states they would not have chosen either option, without reasoning based on outcomes or probabilities.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the maximum outcomes first (which differ: B has 2500, A has 2400), and thus would prefer B. The individual, however, does not consider the outcomes at all, stating that risk differences are marginal and that they would not have chosen either option. There is no mention of maximum or minimum outcomes, nor any justification based on favorable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information relevant to the reason (differences in maximum outcomes) was not considered, and the justification for the choice (if any) does not align with the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

